---
layout: layouts/staff.njk
staffPage: settings
staffNum: "07"
staffTitle: Settings
staffHeading: How this <b>works</b>
staffHint: some of these change what the public sees
---
{#- Tabs rather than one long page: these groups have different audiences and
   different blast radii. Account is about you. Languages and API keys change
   what a public website serves. Keeping them apart makes that difference
   visible before you touch anything, instead of after. -#}
<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="account"
          aria-selected="true" data-i18n="set.account">Account</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="languages"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="set.languages">Languages</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="keys"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="set.keys">API keys</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="embeds"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="set.embeds">Embeds</button>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================= ACCOUNT -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="account" role="tabpanel">
  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.signedInAs">Signed in as</h3>
      <p id="setEmail">—</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      {#- Access owns the identity, so there is no password here to change and
         pretending otherwise would send people looking for a control that
         does not exist. -#}
      <p class="note-inline" data-i18n="set.identityNote">Your sign-in is managed by Cloudflare Access. Changing your email address or password is done there, not here.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.yourAccess">Your access</h3>
      <p data-i18n="set.accessNote">What this account is allowed to do. Changed by an administrator.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <div class="role-tags" id="setRoles"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================================== LANGUAGES -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="languages" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  {#- YOUR language first, and marked as personal, because everything below it
     changes what strangers see. Reading order is blast radius: smallest
     first. -#}
  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.yourLanguage">Your language</h3>
      <p data-i18n="set.yourLanguageDesc">Translates this console and opens the milestone editor in the same language.</p>
      <p class="note-inline" data-i18n="set.yourLanguageNote">Affects only you.
        It changes nothing a visitor sees, whatever your role.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <select id="setPrefLang" class="lang-pick"></select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="note" data-i18n-html="set.publicWarn"><b>Everything below changes what partner websites serve.</b> A language
    switched on here is offered to visitors; one switched off disappears from
    the public API. Translations you have already written are kept either way.</p>

  <div class="set-row set-row-block">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.publishedLanguages">Published languages</h3>
      <p data-i18n="set.publishedDesc">Switch a language on to translate into it and serve it on partner sites. The site's default language cannot be switched off.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control" id="setLangList"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================================================ KEYS -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="keys" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <p class="note" data-i18n-html="set.keysNote">An API key lets a partner website read your <b>published</b> milestones and
    goal totals at build time. It can read nothing else — no contacts, no
    interactions, no drafts.</p>

  <div class="ms-bar key-create">
    <input type="text" id="setKeyName" class="key-name" maxlength="80" data-i18n-attr="placeholder:set.keyPlaceholder"
           placeholder="What is this key for? e.g. chaseroush.com build">
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="setKeyAdd"
            data-i18n="set.createKey">Create key</button>
  </div>

  {#- Shown once, on creation, and never again — the database stores only a
     hash. Deliberately loud, because there is no second chance to copy it. -#}
  <div class="key-reveal" id="setKeyReveal" hidden>
    <h4 data-i18n="set.keyRevealTitle">Copy this now — it cannot be shown again</h4>
    <code id="setKeyValue"></code>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="setKeyCopy" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
    <p data-i18n-html="set.keyRevealNote">Store it in the partner site's build environment as
       <code>THAUMA_API_KEY</code>. Never in a repository, and never in
       client-side JavaScript.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-list" id="setKeyList"></div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================== EMBEDS -->
{#- The one thing in this console that publishes to people who have not signed
   in to anything. An API key is a credential you hand to one build; an embed
   is a URL anybody can fetch. So the switch comes FIRST, says exactly what it
   does, and everything below it only matters once it is on. -#}
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="embeds" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <p class="note" data-i18n-html="set.embedNote">A widget shows your <b>published</b> goals or roadmap on somebody else's
    website — a sending church, a supporter's blog. It reads the same public
    data as the API and needs no key, because a key in a web page is not a
    secret. Nothing private can appear in one.</p>

  <div class="set-row">
    <div class="set-label">
      <h3 data-i18n="set.embedOn">Allow embedding</h3>
      <p data-i18n="set.embedOnDesc">Off until you turn it on. While it is off, the widget address returns nothing at all — not an error saying you exist.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="set-control">
      <label class="switch">
        <input type="checkbox" id="setEmbedOn">
        <span data-i18n="set.embedOnLabel">Anyone may embed my progress</span>
      </label>
      <p class="rolegate" id="setEmbedNotAdmin" hidden
         data-i18n="set.embedAdminOnly">An administrator changes this.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="setEmbedRest" hidden>
    <div class="set-row">
      <div class="set-label">
        <h3 data-i18n="set.embedLook">Colours</h3>
        <p data-i18n="set.embedLookDesc">Saved here, so a page that embedded you last year picks up a change without anyone editing it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="set-control emb-look">
        <label class="emb-field">
          <span data-i18n="set.embedAccent">Accent</span>
          <span class="emb-colour">
            <input type="color" id="setEmbedAccent" value="#6D4AFF">
            <input type="text" id="setEmbedAccentHex" class="emb-hex"
                   maxlength="7" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Accent colour hex">
          </span>
        </label>
        <label class="emb-field">
          <span data-i18n="set.embedTheme">Background</span>
          <select id="setEmbedTheme">
            <option value="auto" data-i18n="set.embedAuto">Match the page</option>
            <option value="light" data-i18n="set.embedLight">Always light</option>
            <option value="dark" data-i18n="set.embedDark">Always dark</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="set-row set-row-block">
      <div class="set-label">
        <h3 data-i18n="set.embedBuild">The code to paste</h3>
        <p data-i18n="set.embedBuildDesc">Choose what it shows, then copy. The preview is the real widget reading your real numbers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="set-control">
        <div class="emb-opts">
          <label class="emb-field">
            <span data-i18n="set.embedWidget">Show</span>
            <select id="setEmbedWidget">
              <option value="goal" data-i18n="set.embedGoal">Giving progress</option>
              <option value="roadmap" data-i18n="set.embedRoadmap">Roadmap</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="emb-field">
            <span data-i18n="set.embedLang">Language</span>
            <select id="setEmbedLang"></select>
          </label>
          <label class="emb-field">
            <span data-i18n="set.embedLimit">Rows</span>
            <input type="number" id="setEmbedLimit" min="0" max="20" step="1" value="0">
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="emb-split">
          <div class="emb-codewrap">
            <pre class="emb-code" id="setEmbedCode"></pre>
            <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="setEmbedCopy"
                    data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
          </div>
          {#- A real iframe, not a mock. The widget has a shadow root and its
             own stylesheet, and rendering it directly in this page would
             prove nothing about how it behaves as a guest somewhere else. -#}
          <div class="emb-preview">
            <div class="emb-preview-label" data-i18n="set.embedPreview">Preview</div>
            <iframe id="setEmbedFrame" title="Embed preview" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
